		<!--
			Engine fire visuals (visual layer only, nothing here feeds back into the systems).
			- Driven by the fire itself, not by the detection, and by one signal only: L:A32NX_ENG_n_ON_FIRE, "the engine
			  is burning" (systems.wasm SetOnFireModule, fire_and_smoke_protection.rs): set by the flyPad fire failure,
			  cleared when the failure is removed or when an AGENT discharge puts the fire out (1/2 chance per bottle).
			  Its copy in the sim's ENG ON FIRE:n (a380_systems_wasm fire.rs, read by the fire detection) is not read
			  here: the flames went on after the failure removal with it in the code (sim 2026-10-09). A FIRE TEST shows
			  nothing: it lights the warnings only, there is no fire (FCOM DSC-26-20-20 TEST pb: chime, MASTER WARN,
			  ECAM, FIRE pb, SQUIB/DISCH and ENG MASTER panel FIRE lights).
			- The effect stays on after the engine shutdown, until the fire is out (FCOM DSC-26-20-20: the FIRE light
			  "remains on, until the fire is extinguished, regardless of the position of the ENG FIRE pb").
			- Every effect is ANDed with L:A32NX_CONFIG_SITUATION_FX, the flyPad Settings > Sim Options switch "Situation
			  Visual Effects" (default on), written by the flyPad from its persistent setting CONFIG_SITUATION_FX.
			- Look (design choice, the FCOM gives no visual description of a fire): the stock MSFS 2024 visual effect graph
			  FX_Fire_1_Small (flames) and FX_Smoke_Fire (smoke, added on the user's request 2026-10-09) of the package fs-base-effects (VisualEffectLibs/Asobo/Base), its GUID being the one
			  stored in the .spb file, where the SDK template GUIDs (contrails, heat, ballast) are found too. It hangs, with
			  no offset, on the exhaust node of each engine: LEFT1 = engine 1 (left outer) ... RIGHT4 = engine 4 (right
			  outer), as the node positions of A380_WINGS.gltf show. FX offsets proved unreliable on the jettison plume.
			- Engine 2 node (design choice): FX_EXHAUST_RIGHT2, a child of the left inner engine bone (INBOARD_ENG_LH) in
			  both A380_WINGS.gltf (LOD00) and A380_WINGS_LOD01.gltf, despite its name. FX_EXHAUST_LEFT2, at the same
			  position (x = +15.04 m), is only in LOD00, at the scene root: its effects vanished at LOD01. Every engine 2
			  effect of this file (fire, smoke, damage, oil leak, contrails) and the aircraft.cfg heat haze use RIGHT2.
			  A380_WINGS_LOD02.gltf has no exhaust node at all (no engine effect there, for any engine).
